The REAL tool path works — pixel(5,4) IS white! So why did the test fail? In the test, the pixel loop:

```dart
final on = stitchGlyphPixels(letters[i]);
for (final (dx, dy) in on) {
 final pixel = composite.getPixel(origin.$1 + dx, origin.$2 + dy);
``

stitchGlyphPixels returns (x, y) pairs. Tile 0 origin (0,0) → pixel (1,0) means dx=1, dy=0 → composite pixel (0+1, 0+0) = (1,0) — NOT (5,4)!! The test forgot the PLATE OFFSET: glyph pixels are relative to the glyph origin which sits at origin + stitchPlatePadding. In `_drawGlyph` the glyph draws at `originX + stitchPlatePadding, originY + stitchPlatePadding` (4,4). The test adds only the tile origin. Fix the TEST: check pixels at origin + padding + glyph offset. Also fix the cosmetic reason string.

